      "chunk": "The logistics of extracting and transporting this natural gas involve substantial infrastructure investments, particularly in pipeline construction. Estimates suggest that building the necessary pipeline to transport gas from the drilling sites to the port could cost upwards of $4 billion. This project would require a collaborative effort between the public and private sectors to secure funding and long-term commitments from gas customers. The involvement of Asian countries in financing the pipeline remains a critical question, as their participation could alleviate some of the financial burdens and ensure a steady supply of natural gas to meet their energy needs.",
